        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758306,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo Game Boy, released in 1989, revolutionized handheld gaming. This iconic 8-bit console, developed by Nintendo R&D1, prioritized affordability, durability, and long battery life over cutting-edge technology, opting for a monochrome display and an 8-bit processor. Initially priced at $89.99, it quickly became a global phenomenon, selling over 118 million units across its variants. \n\nThe Game Boy utilized ROM cartridges, with early limitations overcome by innovative memory bank controllers allowing for games up to 1MB. Bundled with the immensely popular *Tetris*, it broadened the appeal of video games beyond traditional audiences. Later successes included the groundbreaking *Pokémon* series, which sold over 46 million copies. Redesigned models like the Game Boy Pocket and Light followed, and its backward compatibility with Game Boy Color games solidified its legacy as a cornerstone of gaming history."
          },
